<p>Israeli air strikes hit locations in eastern Lebanon’s Bekaa Valley, including the Baalbek area. Israel’s military said it targeted Hezbollah “command centres” and related sites. Lebanese authorities and media said at least 10 people were killed and dozens were wounded; some outlets put the death toll at 12 and said injuries rose into the 30s. Al Jazeera also reported strikes in southern Lebanon, including near Ein el-Hilweh, the country’s largest Palestinian refugee camp. It also said Israel struck a building in the country’s east.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/iyIp0LId_AaIYJoNpQOm7NEUDyYyTrc5eWOnBiSWI6NIk7TnBT_mxg86taNk0h7-ui0zp4sAUtqa_8QdU3oY2_WqTGtjDIlDnM_Tl7lVfa4OFrRlhkbq6vMjKEpZKjKb_VmIArXBeL4spgg1DqTSLnJZFEyJiZtVdJAsLdWfD3pzJPYvlck1TCPaeDqzvzQeGERceWYSOS6acaPycIPFDdTFyz7VKqncEmGyPW-A27sqVpL_rMItO7kJb1cF4OvbRMK27yVMmk4yXpb-oQ' alt='The city of Baalbek in Lebanon; Israel said it struck Hezbollah command centres in the area.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Casualties (health ministry): Lebanon’s health ministry said the Bekaa Valley strikes killed at least 10 people and wounded 24, including three children among the wounded.</li><li>Ein el-Hilweh context: Lebanese media, as cited by Al Jazeera, said a strike hit near Ein el-Hilweh — Lebanon’s largest Palestinian refugee camp — and also reported an attack on a building in the country’s east.</li><li>Reported Hezbollah loss: Two security sources cited in reporting said senior Hezbollah official Hussein Yaghi was among those killed.</li><li>Intensity in the east: Several outlets described the Bekaa Valley strikes as among the deadliest reported in eastern Lebanon in recent weeks.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Israeli military: The military said it struck Hezbollah “command centres” and related sites in the Baalbek area of the Bekaa Valley. (<a href='https://www.dw.com/en/israel-says-it-hit-hezbollah-sites-in-eastern-lebanon/a-76068525'>DW</a>)</li><li>Lebanese health ministry: The ministry